{
  "version": "Notebook/1.0",
  "items": [
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## NTLM Security Monitoring Dashboard\n---\n\nComprehensive monitoring of NTLM authentication activity, brute-force attacks, and security posture across your environment. This dashboard provides real-time detection of credential attacks, lateral movement, and tracks NTLM deprecation progress.\n\n**Last Updated:** July 23, 2026  \n**Data Sources:** SecurityEvent, Event (System / NTLM Operational logs), IdentityLogonEvents, DeviceLogonEvents, DeviceNetworkEvents, DeviceFileEvents, DeviceEvents, ThreatIntelIndicators, W3CIISLog\n\n⚠️ **NTLM is a legacy protocol vulnerable to Pass-the-Hash, coerced-auth, and relay attacks. Use this dashboard to monitor deprecation progress, detect active attacks, and remove NTLM dependencies.**\n\n### 📡 Supported NTLM Monitoring Events\n| Event ID | Source | Type | Description | Key Fields |\n|----------|--------|------|-------------|------------|\n| **4624 / 4625** | Security | Auth | Logon Success/Failure (LmPackageName = NTLM version) | Account, IP, LogonType |\n| **4776** | Security (DC) | NTLM | Credential validation on DC | TargetUserName, Workstation, IP |\n| **4769** | Security (DC) | Kerberos | TGS Request (SPN capture — fallback analysis) | ServiceName (SPN) |\n| **5145** | Security | SMB | File share access (coercion pipe hunt) | ShareName, RelativeTargetName |\n| **8001** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Outbound Client NTLM (audit) | ClientProcessName, TargetName |\n| **8002** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Inbound NTLM audit (local/loopback) | Server, User |\n| **8003** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Member server inbound NTLM audit | ProcessName, ClientName |\n| **8004** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | DC audit — secure-channel NTLM | Secure channel name |\n| **8005** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | DC audit — direct NTLM to DC | Target, User |\n| **8006** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | DC audit — cross-trust NTLM | Trusted domain |\n| **4001–4006** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | NTLM **blocked** (replaces 8001–8006 after enforcement) | Reason |\n| **4020** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Enhanced client outbound (Win11 24H2 / Srv 2025+) | SPN, NegFlags, Reason |\n| **4022** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Enhanced server inbound (2025+) | SPN, NTLM version |\n| **4030** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Enhanced cross-domain NTLM (2025+) | Trust, User |\n| **4032** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Enhanced DC audit — **detects NTLMv1 from DC log alone** (2025+) | NTLM version, SPN |\n| **4021 / 4023 / 4031 / 4033** | System / NTLM Operational | NTLM | Enhanced **blocked** events (2025+) | Reason |\n\n**⚠️ Deprecate / de-prioritize:** NTLMv1 detection based solely on `4624 LmPackageName` on Srv 2016/2019/2022 — replace with **event 4032** on 2025 DCs. Any tile still querying the retired `ThreatIntelligenceIndicator` table must be migrated to **`ThreatIntelIndicators`**."
      },
      "name": "text - header"
    },
    {
      "type": 1,
      "content": {
        "json": "## 📋 Requirements & Prerequisites\n\n### **Required Data Sources**\n\n| Data Source | Purpose | Collection Method |\n|-------------|---------|-------------------|\n| **SecurityEvent** | Windows Security logs (Event IDs 4624, 4625, 4769, 4776, 5145) | Azure Monitor Agent (AMA) or Log Analytics Agent |\n| **Event** (System / NTLM Operational) | NTLM audit events 8001–8006, 4001–4006, 4020–4033 | AMA + `Microsoft-Windows-NTLM/Operational` channel |\n| **IdentityLogonEvents** | Active Directory authentication activity (MDI) | Microsoft Defender for Identity (MDI) sensors |\n| **DeviceLogonEvents** | Endpoint logon events (MDE) | Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (MDE) |\n| **DeviceNetworkEvents / DeviceFileEvents / DeviceEvents** | Hash-exfil / VM-snapshot theft / LSASS tamper hunts | MDE Advanced Hunting |\n| **ThreatIntelIndicators** | Current TI table (replaces retired `ThreatIntelligenceIndicator`) | Sentinel TI connectors (TAXII / MDTI / custom) |\n| **W3CIISLog** | External NTLM surface probing on IIS/Exchange/RDWeb/ADFS/AD CS | IIS logs → Log Analytics |\n\n### **Required Event IDs**\n\n| Event ID | Description | Log Source | Criticality |\n|----------|-------------|------------|-------------|\n| **4624** | Successful logon (LmPackageName reveals NTLM version) | Security | ✅ Required |\n| **4625** | Failed logon (SubStatus `0xC0000418` = NTLM blocked) | Security | ✅ Required |\n| **4776** | NTLM credential validation on DC — baseline / top-talkers | Security (DC) | ✅ Required |\n| **4769** | Kerberos TGS Request (SPN + fallback analysis) | Security (DC) | ✅ Required |\n| **5145** | SMB share access (coercion pipe hunt: efsrpc, spoolss, netdfs, …) | Security | 🟠 Recommended |\n| **8001** | Outbound Client NTLM audit (process name) | NTLM Operational | 🟠 Recommended |\n| **8002** | Inbound NTLM audit — local/loopback | NTLM Operational | 🟠 Recommended |\n| **8003** | Inbound NTLM audit — member server (domain accts) | NTLM Operational | 🟠 Recommended |\n| **8004 / 8005 / 8006** | DC audit — secure-channel / direct / cross-trust NTLM | NTLM Operational (DC) | 🟠 Recommended |\n| **4001–4006** | NTLM **blocked** counterparts to 8001–8006 | NTLM Operational | 🟠 Recommended once enforcing |\n| **4020** | Enhanced client outbound (Win11 24H2 / Srv 2025+) — includes SPN, NegFlags, fallback reason | NTLM Operational | 🟢 New (2025+) |\n| **4022** | Enhanced server inbound (2025+) — SPN, NTLM version | NTLM Operational | 🟢 New (2025+) |\n| **4030** | Enhanced cross-domain NTLM (2025+) | NTLM Operational | 🟢 New (2025+) |\n| **4032** | Enhanced DC audit — **finally detects NTLMv1 from DC log alone** (2025+) | NTLM Operational (DC) | 🟢 New (2025+) — Priority |\n| **4021 / 4023 / 4031 / 4033** | Enhanced **blocked** events (2025+) | NTLM Operational | 🟢 New (2025+) |\n| ⚠️ **Deprecate** | Old NTLMv1 hunts using only 4624 LmPackageName on 2016/2019/2022 → migrate to 4032 on 2025 DCs | — | 🟡 Retire |\n\n---\n\n### **📡 XPath Queries for Data Collection Rules (DCR)**\n\nConfigure these XPath queries in your Azure Monitor Agent Data Collection Rules to collect the required logs:\n\n**Security Log - NTLM/Kerberos Authentication + Coercion Pipe Access:**\n```\nSecurity!*[System[(EventID=4624 or EventID=4625 or EventID=4648 or EventID=4769 or EventID=4776 or EventID=5145)]]\n```\n\n**Legacy System Log — retained for compatibility:**\n```\nSystem!*[System[(EventID=8001 or EventID=8002 or EventID=8003 or EventID=8004)]]\n```\n\n**NTLM Operational channel — modern audit + block + enhanced events (Win11 24H2 / Srv 2025+):**\n```\nMicrosoft-Windows-NTLM/Operational!*[System[(EventID=8001 or EventID=8002 or EventID=8003 or EventID=8004 or EventID=8005 or EventID=8006 or EventID=4001 or EventID=4002 or EventID=4003 or EventID=4004 or EventID=4005 or EventID=4006 or EventID=4020 or EventID=4021 or EventID=4022 or EventID=4023 or EventID=4030 or EventID=4031 or EventID=4032 or EventID=4033)]]\n```\n\n**Note:** Enable auditing via GPO *Computer Configuration → Windows Settings → Security Settings → Local Policies → Security Options → Network security: Restrict NTLM: Audit \\**. Events 4020–4033 require Windows 11 24H2+ or Windows Server 2025+.\n\n**DCR Configuration Steps:**\n1. Navigate to **Azure Portal** → **Monitor** → **Data Collection Rules**\n2. Create or edit a DCR associated with your Windows servers\n3. Add **Windows Event Logs** as a data source\n4. Select **Custom** and paste the XPath queries above\n5. Set destination to your Log Analytics workspace\n6. Deploy DCR to target VMs via Azure Policy or direct assignment\n\n---\n\n### **Prerequisites**\n\n**1. Windows Systems (Domain Controllers & Member Servers):**\n- ✅ Azure Monitor Agent or Log Analytics Agent installed\n- ✅ Connected to Log Analytics workspace\n- ✅ Advanced Audit Policy enabled:\n  - `Audit Logon` (Success, Failure)\n  - `Audit Account Logon` (Success, Failure)\n  - `Audit Credential Validation` (Success, Failure)\n\n**2. Microsoft Defender for Identity (for IdentityLogonEvents):**\n- ✅ MDI sensors installed on all Domain Controllers\n- ✅ MDI workspace connected to Microsoft Sentinel\n- ✅ IdentityLogonEvents table populated (may take 24-48 hours after deployment)\n\n**3. Microsoft Defender for Endpoint (for DeviceLogonEvents):**\n- ✅ MDE agents deployed to Windows endpoints\n- ✅ MDE workspace connected to Microsoft Sentinel\n- ✅ Advanced hunting data available\n\n**4. Optional: Enhanced NTLM Auditing:**\n- Registry: `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0`\n  - `AuditReceivingNTLMTraffic` = 2 (Dword)\n- Registry: `HKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters`\n  - `AuditNTLMInDomain` = 7 (Dword)\n\n### **Verification Steps**\n\n**Test SecurityEvent collection:**\n```kql\nSecurityEvent\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)\n| where EventID in (4624, 4625)\n| where AuthenticationPackageName has \\\"NTLM\\\"\n| take 10\n```\n\n**Test IdentityLogonEvents collection:**\n```kql\nIdentityLogonEvents\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)\n| where Protocol has \\\"NTLM\\\"\n| take 10\n```\n\n**Test DeviceLogonEvents collection:**\n```kql\nDeviceLogonEvents\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)\n| where Protocol has \\\"NTLM\\\"\n| take 10\n```\n\n⚠️ **Note:** If queries return 0 results, verify agents are installed, audit policies are enabled, and data is flowing to Sentinel. Allow 15-30 minutes for initial data ingestion.\n\n---"
      },
      "name": "text - requirements"
    },
    {
      "type": 9,
      "content": {
        "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
        "parameters": [
          {
            "id": "2f84ed9a-e3ed-498d-8b1e-e0a7e6c89f72",
            "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
            "name": "TimeRange",
            "label": "Time Range",
            "type": 4,
            "isRequired": true,
            "value": {
              "durationMs": 2592000000
            },
            "typeSettings": {
